author ai
group cli
note How one command line becomes an Invocation and runs. The process arguments after the root and the GUI output panel's input line both go through cli::Invocation::parse, which is clap over wire.rs's Command enum, so help and argument errors read the same in both. convert.rs turns the parsed Command into a Request (a Query, an Edit or a repin) of domain values, and cli::exec runs it against the Index and Map through exec.rs's Run, writing its lines to an Output and returning whether the map changed or a Failure. The CLI saves through MapStore and exits with a status; the GUI marks the map unsaved and leaves saving to ctrl+s. The two front ends share everything but the argument splitting, which the shell does for the CLI, and the author they pass: Agent from the CLI, Human from the GUI.

